/T (Space Space is viewed differently by different cultures. In some cultures, people want to be far apart; in other cultures, they want to be close. In some cultures like Arab culture people stand closer to each other; not following this practice is considered impolite and bad etiquette. Americans view personal space as a right and tend to respect this right of others at least 2 feet.)
/E (Space Space is viewed differently by different cultures. In some cultures, people want to be far apart; in other cultures, they want to be close. In some cultures like Arab culture people stand closer to each other; not following this practice is considered impolite and bad etiquette. Americans view personal space as a right and tend to respect this right of others at least 2 feet.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
